raylib
------------------------------------------
raylib is highly inspired by Borland BGI graphics lib and by XNA framework and
it's specially well suited for prototyping, tooling, graphical applications,
embedded systems and education.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.11-1
  libglfw-devel-3.5.1-1bl1
  libglfw3-3.5.1-1bl1
  libraylib-devel-6.2-1bl1
  libraylib620-6.2-1bl1
  pkg-config-3.0.9-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.4-1
  cygport-0.37.11-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libGL-devel-23.3.6-1
  libX11-devel-1.8.13-1
  libglfw-devel-3.5.1-1bl1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/raysan5/raylib

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/raysan5/raylib/archive/refs/tags/6.2.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack raylib-6.2-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./raylib-6.2-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/raylib-6.2-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/raylib-6.2-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libraylib620-6.2-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libraylib-devel-6.2-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(raylib)
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/raylib.README
  /usr/share/doc/raylib/BINDINGS.md
  /usr/share/doc/raylib/CHANGELOG
  /usr/share/doc/raylib/CONTRIBUTING.md
  /usr/share/doc/raylib/CONVENTIONS.md
  /usr/share/doc/raylib/FAQ.md
  /usr/share/doc/raylib/HISTORY.md
  /usr/share/doc/raylib/LICENSE
  /usr/share/doc/raylib/README.md
  /usr/share/doc/raylib/ROADMAP.md
  /usr/share/doc/raylib/SECURITY.md

(libraylib620)
  /usr/bin/cygraylib-620.dll

(libraylib-devel)
  /usr/include/raylib.h
  /usr/include/raymath.h
  /usr/include/rcamera.h
  /usr/include/rlgl.h
  /usr/lib/cmake/raylib/raylib-config-version.cmake
  /usr/lib/cmake/raylib/raylib-config.cmake
  /usr/lib/cmake/raylib/raylib-targets-relwithdebinfo.cmake
  /usr/lib/cmake/raylib/raylib-targets.cmake
  /usr/lib/libraylib.dll.a
  /usr/lib/pkgconfig/raylib.pc

